{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-7980-r4615205","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Potato Curry (Aloo Masala)","sourcePageId":7980,"sourceRevision":"4615205","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:38:40Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Potato%20Curry%20(Aloo%20Masala)&oldid=4615205","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:28.261Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dal recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"34b9903ea6d149754c1bd0e60bf63dd1bfdc317b316dfbdc186b9f8a5f6f66b9","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Side dish recipes|servings=4-6|time=20 minutes|difficulty=3|Image=[[File:An Aesthetic Potato Masala.jpg|300px]]}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian recipes]] | [[Cookbook:Vegan cuisine|Vegan]]\n\n'''Potato masala''' (Tamil: ''uralai kizhangu masala'') is a potato dish often served alongside [[Cookbook:Roti|roti]] or folded inside a [[Cookbook:Dosa|dosa]]. The dosa and aloo masala combination, widely eaten in South [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|India]], is known as ''masala dosa''. [[Cookbook:Coconut Chutney|Coconut chutney]] is a common accompaniment.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[cookbook:oil|oil]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Mustard Seed|mustard seed]]\n* ½ tablespoon [[Cookbook:Chickpea|chana]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dhal]] (optional)\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], chopped thin\n* 4-5 split green [[Cookbook:Chilli pepper|chillies]]\n* 4 large [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], cubed and par-boiled\n* 1 pinch of [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n==Procedure==\n# Heat oil.\n# [[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sautée]] the mustard seed first, then add chana dhal, curry leaves, onion and chillies. \n# Fry until the onions begin to change color.\n# Add potatoes.\n# Sprinkle the turmeric evenly and stir well to mix all the ingredients\n# Cover and cook on a medium flame for about 5 minutes, stirring well, until the potatoes become very soft and somewhat mashed.\n# Season with salt to taste.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes|Aloo masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using potato|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes|Aloo masala]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Potato Curry (Aloo Masala)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tablespoon oil","sourceText":"1 tablespoon oil","amountText":"1 tablespoon oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ teaspoon mustard seed","sourceText":"½ teaspoon mustard seed","amountText":"½ teaspoon mustard seed","amount":nu